(GOVERNMENT OF INDIA - SCHOLARSHIP NOTIFICATION) Tj T*
T*
(DEPARTMENT OF HIGHER EDUCATION & SOCIAL WELFARE) Tj T*
(NOTIFICATION NO: EDN/SCH/2026-8840) Tj T*
(SCHEME: NATIONAL MERIT-CUM-MEANS SCHOLARSHIP SCHEME \(NMMSS\) 2026-27) Tj T*
T*
(1. OBJECTIVE AND PURPOSE:) Tj T*
(The objective of the scheme is to award scholarships to meritorious students of) Tj T*
(economically weaker sections to arrest their drop-out at class VIII and encourage) Tj T*
(them to continue their education at secondary stage.) Tj T*
T*
(2. IMPORTANT DATES & TIMELINES:) Tj T*
(- Portal Opening Date: October 15, 2026) Tj T*
(- Last Date for Online Application Submission: November 30, 2026) Tj T*
(- Institution Level Verification Deadline: December 15, 2026) Tj T*
(- State Nodal Officer Verification Deadline: December 31, 2026) Tj T*
(- State-level Examination Date: January 18, 2027) Tj T*
T*
(3. ELIGIBILITY CRITERIA:) Tj T*
(- The candidate must be a regular student enrolled in recognized government / aided schools.) Tj T*
(- Minimum Academic Qualification: 55% marks or equivalent grade in Class VII annual examination.) Tj T*
(- Parental Annual Income: Total annual income from all sources must not exceed Rs. 2,50,000.) Tj T*
(- Students studying in Kendriya Vidyalayas and Jawahar Navodaya Vidyalayas are NOT eligible.) Tj T*
T*
(4. REQUIRED CERTIFICATES & DOCUMENTS:) Tj T*
(- Verified Income Certificate issued by Revenue Authority \(Tahsildar/MRO\) dated after April 2026.) Tj T*
(- Class VII Annual Exam Marksheet certified by School Principal.) Tj T*
(- Student Aadhaar Card copy \(or Aadhaar Enrolment Slip\).) Tj T*
(- Caste / Category Certificate \(SC/ST/OBC\), if applicable.) Tj T*
(- Bank Account Passbook \(active account linked with Aadhaar in student name\).) Tj T*
(- Recent passport-sized color photograph \(3.5 cm x 4.5 cm\).) Tj T*
T*
(5. FINANCIAL BENEFIT & APPLICATION FEE:) Tj T*
(- Scholarship Amount: Rs. 12,000 per annum \(Rs. 1,000 per month\).) Tj T*
(- Application Processing Fee: NIL \(Application is completely free of charge\).) Tj T*
T*
(6. HOW TO APPLY \(STEP-BY-STEP\):) Tj T*
(Step 1: Register on the National Scholarship Portal \(scholarships.gov.in\).) Tj T*
(Step 2: Fill in personal, educational, and bank details accurately.) Tj T*
(Step 3: Upload scanned copies of required certificates \(PDF/JPEG max 200KB\).) Tj T*
(Step 4: Submit application and submit printed copy to School Principal.) Tj T*
T*
(7. WARNINGS & CONSEQUENCES OF FALSE INFORMATION:) Tj T*
(- Submission of forged income or caste certificates will lead to immediate cancellation) Tj T*
(  and recovery of disbursed amounts along with legal action under IPC Section 420.) Tj T*
(- Late applications submitted after November 30, 2026 will be rejected automatically.) Tj T*
(- NOTE: Hostel allowance and private tuition fees are NOT covered under this scheme.) Tj T*
ET
